## How we work

Specs live in files, not in chat. Chat is gone next session; files aren't.

- `docs/scoping.md` — project-level why and what. The source of constraints.
- `docs/specs/` — how the system behaves today. One file per capability.
- `docs/changes/` — one numbered folder per proposed change, containing `proposal.md` (why, and what changes) and `tasks.md` (the steps). Larger changes also get `design.md` (how).
- `docs/changes/archive/` — completed changes.

## Guardrails

1. No implementation code without an approved proposal in `docs/changes/`. If asked for code outside an approved change, write the proposal first and ask.
2. Work the task list in order. Stop at the end of a change with `results.md`, or at a stop condition, not after each task.
3. When a change is complete:
   - Update `docs/specs/` to match what is now true.
   - Update `docs/scoping.md` (requirement ticks, milestone status, decision index).
   - Write `results.md` (measurements, and screenshots or GIFs when the change touches a frontend).
   - Move the change folder to `docs/changes/archive/`.
4. Specs describe behaviour. Proposals record decisions. Don't mix them.
5. Work on a branch, never on `main`. A change lands as a pull request. One branch per change, opened with `gh pr create`.
6. Working docs and artifacts stay out of any published package or build.
